      {
        "question": "项目历史上有哪些被拒绝的特性提案及理由？",
        "seconds": 125.68,
        "status": "ok",
        "answer": [
          {
            "text": "PR #1 提议为 itsdangerous 增加 marrow.templating 支持；GitHub API 显示该 PR 的 `merged` 为 `false`，即未被合并。",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "Evidence:2043dc72d6dca083cee42f7f05d45385aefd62a97d070198343b511f217accb2",
              "Evidence:b1defd9e812e3434a208b0f54989e71f7d53268fae0ef0e49109ae66f28285ab"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "维护者 mitsuhiko 拒绝 marrow.templating 方向，理由是他仍记得上一次统一模板语言 API 尝试很糟糕、不想再次参与；他建议由另一个库为 marrow 实现 entrypoints。",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "Evidence:6f44b66263e6e29a2126d09077df306d9e4b2b2f3ce12429614ad4b9eb3e302f"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Issue #25 提议允许设置默认 secret key，理由是每次使用 signer 都传这些信息不 DRY；提案还提到其基于 Django 的签名模块。",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "Evidence:b2749213f418e67b08f40df1e128c86270aa23b10da6247f0a851d4c50316509"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "维护者 mitsuhiko 拒绝该 secret key 方向，理由是 itsdangerous 是独立库、与 Django 无关，不会加入在特定环境中自动生效的 magic。",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "Evidence:dd147f2b912e3f63f0deb251b4ba4dc681e5c4e21cf1071cda9c7f4d6af6468f"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "对于 CRIME/BREACH 式攻击的担忧，mitsuhiko 拒绝在 itsdangerous 内处理，理由是其dangerous 只负责签名，相关问题应在 SSL 层解决，并建议在数据负载中加入随机 salt。",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "Evidence:37e060690a9fa6a86603e18c7ee5f0002e64c11ff4cf9a3adc33b7dfca3fd1fb"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Issue #40 的过期日期需求被指向自定义 Serializer 子类；维护者称这是编写自己的 Serializer 子类的好案例。",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "Evidence:afdb4b825c27470a3bcb1e10d813b159190e9854a9d4f987c01492872feba1e1"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Issue #45 请求提供接口来延长已签发 token 的过期时间；回答称不可行，因为过期时间在 token 本身，修改任何值都会得到完全不同的 token，替代方案是使用不过期的 refresh token 来签发新 token。",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "Evidence:20ae22e9e06f70a984ed11b646634627f051ff5ebfd7f3cb3da9359e9ac0f6df",
              "Evidence:459c638eb22288db2affb0cf214008dbf8aad8d9affa4300c8b66adac242e798"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "对于废弃 itsdangerous 的提议，mitsuhiko 表示 JWT 难以安全使用，且不会因此废弃 itsdangerous。",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "Evidence:f57657ab6264aa9811c4f2a449fd02cbd6277f623f0a32ce23a2674506fdd82c"
            ]
          }
        ],
        "links": [
          "https://api.github.com/repos/pallets/itsdangerous/pulls/1",
          "https://github.com/pallets/itsdangerous/issues/25",
          "https://github.com/pallets/itsdangerous/issues/25#issuecomment-21777893",
          "https://github.com/pallets/itsdangerous/issues/26#issuecomment-23160780",
          "https://github.com/pallets/itsdangerous/issues/40#issuecomment-209083922",
          "https://github.com/pallets/itsdangerous/issues/45",
          "https://github.com/pallets/itsdangerous/issues/45#issuecomment-148831232",
          "https://github.com/pallets/itsdangerous/issues/54#issuecomment-161721273",
          "https://github.com/pallets/itsdangerous/pull/1",
          "https://github.com/pallets/itsdangerous/pull/1#issuecomment-1434107"
        ],
        "paths": 32,
        "error": null,
        "cited_evidence": [
          {
            "evidence_id": "Evidence:2043dc72d6dca083cee42f7f05d45385aefd62a97d070198343b511f217accb2",
            "dataset_id": "dataset:0c94c5af1f7f64c628c4a7fe05b496647ad8ef760e18eee01287fd43f1ea3ef2",
            "source_id": "SourceDocument:7d11a1eecc6464a7b42a63915746f33a52e3e61ea68a5817d7d8f3acc6fc0504",
            "start": 8,
            "end": 114,
            "quote": "I've added marrow.templating support; one simple function, an entry point, and no additional dependencies.",
            "url": "https://github.com/pallets/itsdangerous/pull/1",
            "author": "amcgregor",
            "time": "2011-06-24T17:58:21Z",
            "text_sha256": "2318ad848402e39388bc815b82df6134d7a9d23f9bbd2fe601cca1be7e1a4d93"
          },
          {
            "evidence_id": "Evidence:afdb4b825c27470a3bcb1e10d813b159190e9854a9d4f987c01492872feba1e1",
            "dataset_id": "dataset:0c94c5af1f7f64c628c4a7fe05b496647ad8ef760e18eee01287fd43f1ea3ef2",
            "source_id": "SourceDocument:503180ab3f3029f7befcd7e2fa4d8e654311557c2933205da7d7ded65f2eb7c9",
            "start": 0,
            "end": 61,
            "quote": "This is a good case for writing your own Serializer subclass.",
            "url": "https://github.com/pallets/itsdangerous/issues/40#issuecomment-209083922",
            "author": "davidism",
            "time": "2016-04-12T20:11:04Z",
            "text_sha256": "16d8c8c5664b92c521f8acc85231014c2da87ec6213dea6c097ffd86f551514d"
          },
          {
            "evidence_id": "Evidence:dd147f2b912e3f63f0deb251b4ba4dc681e5c4e21cf1071cda9c7f4d6af6468f",
            "dataset_id": "dataset:0c94c5af1f7f64c628c4a7fe05b496647ad8ef760e18eee01287fd43f1ea3ef2",
            "source_id": "SourceDocument:1b4494b3bff401d6aaa9db6c37ce625e3beffa84ae9f9e4d533431d8148afd34",
            "start": 0,
            "end": 167,
            "quote": "Itsdangerous is a separate library and has nothing to do with django.  Definitely not going to add magic that kicks in if the library is used in a certain environment.",
            "url": "https://github.com/pallets/itsdangerous/issues/25#issuecomment-21777893",
            "author": "mitsuhiko",
            "time": "2013-07-30T08:59:55Z",
            "text_sha256": "fa79c2644f8b31048341760e9742a8dae9bcaf55eadef233356b449f5095c136"
          },
          {
            "evidence_id": "Evidence:b1defd9e812e3434a208b0f54989e71f7d53268fae0ef0e49109ae66f28285ab",
            "dataset_id": "dataset:0c94c5af1f7f64c628c4a7fe05b496647ad8ef760e18eee01287fd43f1ea3ef2",
            "source_id": "SourceDocument:25f54c54c4a876f424f3a3f64097e0b324f0c1fd7b556c7470034eb9e52b79d2",
            "start": 10871,
            "end": 11028,
            "quote": "  \"merge_commit_sha\": \"80b9b81f9109ffa64facca0e5d9a7ee0032d9505\",\n  \"mergeable\": false,\n  \"mergeable_state\": \"dirty\",\n  \"merged\": false,\n  \"merged_at\": null,",
            "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/pallets/itsdangerous/pulls/1",
            "author": null,
            "time": null,
            "text_sha256": "0553ea4afdcc27720b47c974a3002f46e22d334fc7a708cf9430ee8a5839e855"
          },
          {
            "evidence_id": "Evidence:6f44b66263e6e29a2126d09077df306d9e4b2b2f3ce12429614ad4b9eb3e302f",
            "dataset_id": "dataset:0c94c5af1f7f64c628c4a7fe05b496647ad8ef760e18eee01287fd43f1ea3ef2",
            "source_id": "SourceDocument:1f9c9b5fcde53e97d583d4f2613b5b92e60261bbbc2f38142b04a1de994fcd51",
            "start": 0,
            "end": 337,
            "quote": "I don't want to step into that particular direction with the library for the time being. Instead why not have a second library that implements the entrypoints for marrow if that is necessary? I still remember the last attempt of an unified templating language API and it was horrible, I don't want to be involved with that a second time.",
            "url": "https://github.com/pallets/itsdangerous/pull/1#issuecomment-1434107",
            "author": "mitsuhiko",
            "time": "2011-06-24T18:09:09Z",
            "text_sha256": "440226c92d6c6bd8173e4e29bc2213c559f6ff84eee51fa00c2ddc5febe52044"
          },
          {
            "evidence_id": "Evidence:b2749213f418e67b08f40df1e128c86270aa23b10da6247f0a851d4c50316509",
            "dataset_id": "dataset:0c94c5af1f7f64c628c4a7fe05b496647ad8ef760e18eee01287fd43f1ea3ef2",
            "source_id": "SourceDocument:d0a35c98fae3b0c75c58a70ac5d0ea2ac0ba2312f1de2cfffd7a40466c02816b",
            "start": 0,
            "end": 280,
            "quote": "Especially since this is based on Django's signing module.\n\nAlternatively, you could let us set a default secret key to use, which would be the more generally useful implementation.\n\nIt's just not very DRY to pass this information in everywhere that you use a signer in your code.",
            "url": "https://github.com/pallets/itsdangerous/issues/25",
            "author": "fletom",
            "time": "2013-07-30T03:30:12Z",
            "text_sha256": "51c2824fe9ba43528857c688d45bef4518496ffd0d9b0f65baede27c234cfcd0"
          },
          {
            "evidence_id": "Evidence:37e060690a9fa6a86603e18c7ee5f0002e64c11ff4cf9a3adc33b7dfca3fd1fb",
            "dataset_id": "dataset:0c94c5af1f7f64c628c4a7fe05b496647ad8ef760e18eee01287fd43f1ea3ef2",
            "source_id": "SourceDocument:1d1877913c2654b494964a81a1da80012bb2a44f8681f1c9f0e69968ada332d5",
            "start": 0,
            "end": 283,
            "quote": "I am familiar with the attack.  Itsdangerous signs, it does nothing else.  Whatever SSL does it out of the focus of this library.  Add a random salt to your data payload if you want to defeat that.  I believe that this issue should be solved on the SSL layer and not in itsdangerous.",
            "url": "https://github.com/pallets/itsdangerous/issues/26#issuecomment-23160780",
            "author": "mitsuhiko",
            "time": "2013-08-23T12:36:22Z",
            "text_sha256": "1a2aa43f0826a917e9cea80f2f152c03088805c9534e00df45464bf347396da9"
          },
          {
            "evidence_id": "Evidence:20ae22e9e06f70a984ed11b646634627f051ff5ebfd7f3cb3da9359e9ac0f6df",
            "dataset_id": "dataset:0c94c5af1f7f64c628c4a7fe05b496647ad8ef760e18eee01287fd43f1ea3ef2",
            "source_id": "SourceDocument:7f831798464a60e31c96ab5fd102097c70416a1f3b97950fedb2375e927c3b97",
            "start": 0,
            "end": 220,
            "quote": "if the token is about to expire, I want to call an interface (or any one can point me in correct way) to extend the expiry time of an already issued token. I am using TimedJSONWebSignatureSerializer to create the tokens.",
            "url": "https://github.com/pallets/itsdangerous/issues/45",
            "author": "ghost",
            "time": "2015-06-19T16:44:20Z",
            "text_sha256": "3a874c48eca693a9c9ffdd2b265f0c51ab4dc33158c77b1acf6d4d3ce9f8c3aa"
          },
          {
            "evidence_id": "Evidence:459c638eb22288db2affb0cf214008dbf8aad8d9affa4300c8b66adac242e798",
            "dataset_id": "dataset:0c94c5af1f7f64c628c4a7fe05b496647ad8ef760e18eee01287fd43f1ea3ef2",
            "source_id": "SourceDocument:bba30a7eb8a6bc975f85fa38f3dee0680568a23b6acfde11a09d44fa34238b65",
            "start": 0,
            "end": 301,
            "quote": "It's impossible to provide a facility like that because the expiration time is in the token itself. When you change any value in the token, you get a completely different token. An alternative implementation would be to issue a refresh token that won't expire and use that to issue new primary tokens.",
            "url": "https://github.com/pallets/itsdangerous/issues/45#issuecomment-148831232",
            "author": "metalgrid",
            "time": "2015-10-16T20:47:42Z",
            "text_sha256": "82e1806e4b98b60503154da7d1801ff798ac8077ac15375b0b0f937f856067d6"
          },
          {
            "evidence_id": "Evidence:f57657ab6264aa9811c4f2a449fd02cbd6277f623f0a32ce23a2674506fdd82c",
            "dataset_id": "dataset:0c94c5af1f7f64c628c4a7fe05b496647ad8ef760e18eee01287fd43f1ea3ef2",
            "source_id": "SourceDocument:f97839150b8f2b891adcfc940a0c1ba7d011b93c0ab154420ecf247cf3febf17",
            "start": 0,
            "end": 226,
            "quote": "I find JWT tricky to use securely which is why I avoid it like the plague whenever I can for my own stuff.  You cannot avoid JWT much for external interoperability obviously but I will not deprecate itsdangerous as a result :)",
            "url": "https://github.com/pallets/itsdangerous/issues/54#issuecomment-161721273",
            "author": "mitsuhiko",
            "time": "2015-12-03T17:19:39Z",
            "text_sha256": "93d0e7303e4c63673753f485b7f7d241c9d54d3c10eca8906fed039149c5b90e"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "question": "为什么移除了 OAuth token 认证？",
